# Dataset

## Source

This dataset was built by combining multiple pothole datasets from
[Roboflow Universe](https://universe.roboflow.com/indian-institute-of-technology-madras-xamot/pothole-detection-huf2x) and [KAGGLE](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/anggadwisunarto/potholes-detection-yolov8), consolidated and
refined for training a YOLOv8 object detection model.

- Roboflow dataset link: **[https://app.roboflow.com/sanyam-singh/smart-pothole-detection-due2d/browse?queryText=&pageSize=50&startingIndex=0&browseQuery=true]**

## Preparation process

- **Merged** images from multiple public pothole datasets (Kaggle and
  Roboflow Universe) into a single unified dataset
- **Removed duplicate images** to avoid data leakage between train/val/test
  splits and reduce redundant training signal
- **Removed blurry / low-quality images** that would not provide a clear,
  learnable visual pattern for the detector
- **Manually annotated** all images with bounding boxes around potholes
  using the Roboflow annotation tool, following a consistent labeling
  standard (tight box around the visible pothole edge; ambiguous cases
  such as shadows, wet patches, and tar repairs excluded)
- Final dataset exported in **YOLOv8 format** (images + label `.txt` files
  + `data.yaml`)

## Class

| Class | Description |
|---|---|
| `pothole` | Visible road surface damage/cavity |

## Usage

The dataset is downloaded directly from Roboflow into the training
environment (Google Colab) rather than stored in this repository, to
keep the repo lightweight. See [`training/`](../training) for the
download + training script.

```python
!pip install roboflow

from roboflow import Roboflow
rf = Roboflow(api_key="7pMaRVVNOSPO7lpdq9HU")
project = rf.workspace("sanyam-singh").project("smart-pothole-detection-due2d")
version = project.version(1)
dataset = version.download("yolov8")
                
```

## Notes

- Dataset version and image counts are tracked on the Roboflow project
  page (linked above) for full reproducibility.